"
File     : PUZ001-1 : TPTP v9.3.1. Released v1.0.0.
Domain   : Puzzles
Problem  : Dreadbury Mansion
Version  : Especial.
           Theorem formulation : Made unsatisfiable.
English  : Someone who lives in Dreadbury Mansion killed Aunt Agatha.
           Agatha, the butler, and Charles live in Dreadbury Mansion,
           and are the only people who live therein. A killer always
           hates his victim, and is never richer than his victim.
           Charles hates no one that Aunt Agatha hates. Agatha hates
           everyone except the butler. The butler hates everyone not
           richer than Aunt Agatha. The butler hates everyone Aunt
           Agatha hates. No one hates everyone. Agatha is not the
           butler. Therefore : Agatha killed herself.
Refs     : [Pel86] Pelletier (1986), Seventy-five Problems for Testing Au
         : [MB88]  Manthey & Bry (1988), SATCHMO: A Theorem Prover Implem
Source   : [TPTP]
Names    :
Status   : Unsatisfiable
Rating   : 0.00 v2.0.0
Syntax   : Number of clauses     :   12 (   5 unt;   2 nHn;  12 RR)
           Number of literals    :   21 (   0 equ;  10 neg)
           Maximal clause size   :    3 (   1 avg)
           Maximal term depth    :    1 (   1 avg)
           Number of predicates  :    4 (   4 usr;   0 prp; 1-2 aty)
           Number of functors    :    3 (   3 usr;   3 con; 0-0 aty)
           Number of variables   :    8 (   0 sgn)
SPC      : CNF_UNS_EPR_NEQ_NHN
Comments : Modified from the [MB88] version to be unsatisfiable, by Geoff
           Sutcliffe.
         : Also known as Who killed Aunt Agatha

Generated by tptp2rsbdd version [version] from tests/data/PUZ001-1.p

Run with:
    rsbdd FILE --prove
"

(
    "agatha (cnf, hypothesis)" lives(agatha) &
    "butler (cnf, hypothesis)" lives(butler) &
    "charles (cnf, hypothesis)" lives(charles) &
    "poorer_killer (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X, Y # -killed(X, Y) | -richer(X, Y)) &
    "different_hates (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X # -hates(agatha, X) | -hates(charles, X)) &
    "no_one_hates_everyone (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X # -hates(X, agatha) | -hates(X, butler) | -hates(X, charles)) &
    "agatha_hates_agatha (cnf, hypothesis)" hates(agatha, agatha) &
    "agatha_hates_charles (cnf, hypothesis)" hates(agatha, charles) &
    "killer_hates_victim (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X, Y # -killed(X, Y) | hates(X, Y)) &
    "same_hates (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X # -hates(agatha, X) | hates(butler, X)) &
    "butler_hates_poor (cnf, hypothesis)" (forall X # -lives(X) | richer(X, agatha) | hates(butler, X)) &
    "prove_neither_charles_nor_butler_did_it (cnf, negated_conjecture)" (killed(butler, agatha) | killed(charles, agatha))
) => false
